  contrast, a_0 flat and unfloored: tilt = 305-282 -- the tilt is the same (it is set by the boost's k-dependence, nu ~ (k/delta)^(1/2)); rising a_0 makes the AMPLITUDE 1e4x worse
  [PASS] 1d the unfloored result is independent of the IC amplitude to < 15% between eps_b = 0.01 and 0.1 (and of Silk damping): deep-MOND growth is an ATTRACTOR, delta ~ t^4, so the tilt is a property of the dynamics, not of the initial conditions   (max |ratio - 1| = 0.054)

========================================================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  a_0 ~ H(z) does put recombination in the deep-MOND regime (nu ~ 30-400 on the acoustic scales), which is the proposal's premise
  and its undoing: the boost is largest where the peculiar gravity is smallest, so a baryon-only universe grows its small scales
  far faster than its large ones and arrives at z = 3 tilted x300 against the measured shape and 1e6-1e9 too strong, on an
  attractor that forgets the initial conditions.  With the
  framework's own derived floor the boost collapses to a constant 8% and nothing grows.  The Boltzmann run is not needed:
  the growth between recombination and z = 3 already fails both ways.  The door is shut.

